  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> resultant x^2 + 1, x^3 + x + 1
resultant x^2 + 1, x^3 + x + 1
  in x: 1
  nonzero: no common root
  check: lc(P)^deg(Q) * product of Q over the roots of P = 1 (agrees)
> discriminant x^5 - 1
discriminant x^5 - 1
  in x (degree 5): 3125
  > 0: distinct roots
  check: lc^(2n-2) * product of (ri - rj)^2 over the roots = 3125 (agrees)
> gcd x^50 - 1, x^25 - 1
gcd x^50 - 1, x^25 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x^4 + x^3 + x^2 + x + 1)*(x^20 + x^15 + x^10 + x^5 + 1)
    = x^25 - 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
